             <img class="blog-hero-image" src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="NEET UG 2026 Registration Start Date – NTA Notification &amp; Apply Online">
             <div class="blog-content">
                 <div class="blog-body">
                     <h1 class="blog-title text-center mb-4">NEET UG 2026 Registration Live: NTA Notification &amp; Your Guide to Apply Online</h1>

                     <p>The wait is over for aspiring medical and dental students across India! The National Testing Agency (NTA) has officially commenced the registration process for the National Eligibility cum Entrance Test (NEET UG) 2026. This national-level examination is the single gateway for admissions to undergraduate medical courses like MBBS, BDS, BAMS, BHMS, BUMS, BVSc &amp; AH, and other related programmes offered by government and private medical colleges nationwide.</p>

                     <p>If you're aiming for a career in medicine, understanding the application timeline, eligibility criteria, and the step-by-step application process is crucial. Here's a comprehensive guide to help you navigate your NEET UG 2026 registration successfully.</p>

                     <div class="highlight-text">
                         <p><strong>Latest Update:</strong> The NEET UG 2026 registration form was released on February 8, 2026, on the official website neet.nta.nic.in. The deadline for submitting the application form and paying fees is March 8, 2026.</p>
                     </div>

                     <h2 class="section-title">NEET UG 2026 Important Dates at a Glance</h2>
                     <p>Staying informed about key dates is paramount. Mark your calendars with these crucial deadlines for NEET UG 2026:</p>
                     <table>
                         <thead>
                             <tr>
                                 <th>Event</th>
                                 <th>Date</th>
                             </tr>
                         </thead>
                         <tbody>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>Online Submission of Application Forms (Start Date)</td>
                                 <td>February 8, 2026</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>Last Date to Fill NEET Registration 2026 Form</td>
                                 <td>March 8, 2026 (up to 9:00 PM)</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>Last Date for Fee Payment</td>
                                 <td>March 8, 2026 (up to 11:50 PM)</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>Application Form Correction Window</td>
                                 <td>March 10 to March 12, 2026</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>NEET 2026 Admit Card Release</td>
                                 <td>Last Week of April 2026 (Expected)</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>NEET UG 2026 Exam Date</td>
                                 <td>May 3, 2026 (2:00 PM to 5:00 PM IST)</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>Display of Provisional Answer Key with OMR &amp; Responses</td>
                                 <td>June 2026 (Expected)</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>NEET 2026 Result Declaration</td>
                                 <td>June 2026 (Expected)</td>
                             </tr>
                         </tbody>
                     </table>

                     <h2 class="section-title">Who Can Apply? NEET UG 2026 Eligibility Criteria</h2>
                     <p>Before proceeding with your application, ensure you meet the essential eligibility requirements set by the NTA. Failing to do so may lead to disqualification later in the admission process.</p>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">1. Age Limit</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">Candidates must have completed 17 years of age on or before December 31, 2026, for the year they are appearing for the NEET-UG examination. There is no upper age limit for NEET UG.</div>
                     </div>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">2. Nationality</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">Interested applicants must be Indian citizens, Non-Resident Indians (NRIs), Overseas Citizens of India (OCIs), Persons of Indian Origin (PIOs), or Foreign Nationals.</div>
                     </div>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">3. Educational Qualifications</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">
                             Students must have passed or be appearing in the 10+2 (or equivalent) examination with Physics, Chemistry, Biology/Biotechnology, and English as core subjects.
                             <p><strong>Minimum Marks:</strong></p>
                             <ul>
                                 <li>General Category: 50% aggregate marks in PCB</li>
                                 <li>OBC/SC/ST: 40% aggregate marks in PCB</li>
                                 <li>Persons with Disability (PH): 45% for General-PH, 40% for Reserved-PH</li>
                             </ul>
                         </div>
                     </div>

                     <h2 class="section-title">Your Step-by-Step Guide to Apply Online</h2>
                     <p>The NEET UG 2026 registration process is entirely online. Follow these steps carefully to ensure a smooth application submission:</p>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">1. Visit the Official Website</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">Go to the official NTA NEET website: <a href="https://neet.nta.nic.in/" target="_blank">neet.nta.nic.in</a>.</div>
                     </div>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">2. New Registration</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">Click on the "NEET 2026 Registration" or "New Registration" link. You will need to provide basic details such as your Name, Date of Birth, Email ID, and Mobile Number to create an account and generate an application number and password.</div>
                     </div>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">3. Fill the Application Form</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">Log in using your newly generated application number and password. Carefully fill in all personal, academic (Class 10 &amp; 12 details), and contact information. Choose your preferred exam cities and the medium of the question paper.</div>
                     </div>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">4. Upload Required Documents</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">Scan and upload the necessary documents as per the prescribed size and format specified in the information bulletin. This typically includes photographs, signature, and other certificates.</div>
                     </div>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">5. Pay the Application Fee</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">Pay the NEET UG 2026 registration fee online using a Debit Card, Credit Card, Net Banking, or UPI. The fee varies by category.</div>
                     </div>

                     <div class="benefit-item">
                         <div class="benefit-title">6. Submit and Download Confirmation</div>
                         <div class="benefit-content">Review all the entered details thoroughly before final submission. After submission, download and print the confirmation page for your records.</div>
                     </div>

                     <h2 class="section-title">Essential Documents for Application</h2>
                     <p>Keep the following documents ready before you begin your online application to avoid last-minute hassles:</p>
                     <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                         <p>✅ Passport-size photograph</p>
                         <p>✅ Postcard-size photograph</p>
                         <p>✅ Candidate's signature (running handwriting)</p>
                         <p>✅ Fingerprints of all fingers (both hands)</p>
                         <p>✅ Class 10 passing certificate</p>
                         <p>✅ Class 12 marksheet (mandatory for repeaters/droppers)</p>
                         <p>✅ Valid Photo ID Proof (Aadhaar Card, PAN Card, Class 12 Admit Card, Bank Passbook, etc.)</p>
                         <p>✅ Aadhaar Card as address proof</p>
                         <p>✅ Category/EWS/PwD Certificate (if applicable, in central format)</p>
                     </div>

                     <h2 class="section-title">NEET UG 2026 Application Fees</h2>
                     <p>The application fee structure for NEET UG 2026 is as follows:</p>
                     <table>
                         <thead>
                             <tr>
                                 <th>Category</th>
                                 <th>Fee</th>
                             </tr>
                         </thead>
                         <tbody>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>General / Open</td>
                                 <td>₹1700</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>OBC / EWS</td>
                                 <td>₹1600</td>
                             </tr>
                             <tr>
                                 <td>SC / ST / PwD / Third Gender</td>
                                 <td>₹1000</td>
                             </tr>
                         </tbody>
                     </table>
                     <p>The fee must be paid online only.</p>

                     <h2 class="section-title">Important Reminders for Aspirants</h2>
                     <div class="subsection-paragraph benefit-card">
                         <p>✅ Apply well before the last date, March 8, 2026, to avoid any technical glitches.</p>
                         <p>✅ Double-check all details entered in the application form before final submission. The NTA will provide a correction window from March 10 to March 12, 2026, for rectifications.</p>
                         <p>✅ Refer only to the official NTA websites (<a href="https://neet.nta.nic.in/" target="_blank">neet.nta.nic.in</a> and <a href="https://nta.ac.in/" target="_blank">nta.ac.in</a>) for accurate and updated information.</p>
                         <p>✅ Keep a copy of the confirmation page and fee receipt for future reference.</p>
                     </div>

                     <p>NEET UG 2026 is your gateway to a rewarding medical career. By carefully following the NTA notification, adhering to the eligibility criteria, and completing the online application process diligently, you can take the first crucial step towards achieving your dreams. Good luck to all the aspirants!</p>
                 </div>
             </div>
       </div>

            
            
